ero Beach's average low shows no clear change: +0.14\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.01 to +0.29) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero. Vero Beach's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.32\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.24 to +0.39), about +2.6\u00b0F since 1943. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.40\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.06 to +0.75) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.37\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.15 to +0.59). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 4 of 12 months. Highs rose in 11 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Vero Beach's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.01 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 53.4 inches a year. The wettest year was 1982 (81.74 in); the driest, 1961 (32.70 in). Vero Beach almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 11 daily record highs, 5 daily record lows"}}